  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Wildlife Without Borders-Western Hemisphere</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Recipient will: (1) complete seasonal surveys providing an updated state of knowledge on the population and conservation status of the orangutan population and their habitat within the Danau Sentarum National Park region; (2) build on current efforts to reduce the rate of conversion and therefore fragmentation of the remaining orangutan habitat in and around the National Park through (a) implementation of a community and government awareness program, (b) development of a conservation plan and collaborative monitoring system, and (c) development of a participatory land-use plan; and (3) continue to strengthen law enforcement on illegal trade, poaching and other threats to orangutans through (a) the development of a joint agreement at the park and/or district level that incorporates local traditional rules, and (b) capacity and knowledge building including a training workshop for 20 law enforcement personnel and two intensive capacity building activities for 30-40 law enforcement personnel.</narrative>
  </description>
